DIFME: connector-common's JWS response filter had no defaults for its condition, so every connector failed to start
unless security.jws.enable and security.jws.response.enable were both set (the other JWS beans default to false).
Same default here: off unless switched on.

--- a/src/main/java/org/mifos/connector/common/interceptor/JWSFilterStrategy.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/mifos/connector/common/interceptor/JWSFilterStrategy.java
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 import org.springframework.web.util.ContentCachingResponseWrapper;
 
 @Component
-@ConditionalOnExpression("${security.jws.enable} and ${security.jws.response.enable}")
+@ConditionalOnExpression("${security.jws.enable:false} and ${security.jws.response.enable:false}")
 @Slf4j
 public class JWSFilterStrategy extends GenericFilterBean {
 
